NSL does not provide a Makefile to build this example of C++ classes,
as the Cplusplus compiler names differ too much from platform to
platform.

To build the class files from the .fm files, the rules are:

Counter.C: Counter.fm
        xfm -c++ -cinclude "<stdlib.h>" Counter.fm

RC.C: RC.fm
        xfm -c++ RC.fm

These will build the .C and .h files for the two C++ classes.

Next, you have to  compile the two classes and the main program
counters.C with your C++ compiler, and finally link

Counters.o RC.o counters.o and the following libraries:
        Fm_c
        Xm
        Xt
        X11
        m
plus any other platform dependent libraries that are necessary to build
a Motif application.

Please refer to a Makefile generated by XFaceMaker for your platform
if you need an example.
